<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="fr">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>{% block title %}{{ setlist.name }}{% endblock %}</title>
    <style>
        {#
            No @page rule. Paper size and margins are set through the Gotenberg builder in
            SetlistPdfRenderer, because a CSS @page margin silently overrides the builder's margin
            fields and the fit arithmetic needs exactly one source of truth for the page box.

            No scale variable either. Shrinking to fit is Chromium's print scale, applied to the
            whole document at render time, so every length shrinks together - including the borders,
            letter-spacing and margins that the old hand-multiplied version left at full size.
        #}
        {#
            The two TTFs travel with the document as uploaded assets, so they are referenced by bare
            filename. Nothing is written to a font cache, which is what made dompdf return a 500 on
            every fresh release directory.

            `font` is the SetlistPdfFont case rather than three loose strings, so the family name and
            its two filenames cannot drift apart.
        #}
        @font-face {
            font-family: '{{ font.cssFamily }}';
            src: url('{{ font.regularFile }}') format('truetype');
            font-weight: normal;
        }
        @font-face {
            font-family: '{{ font.cssFamily }}';
            src: url('{{ font.boldFile }}') format('truetype');
            font-weight: bold;
        }

        body {
            font-family: '{{ font.cssFamily }}', sans-serif;
            color: #1a1a1a;
            margin: 0;
            {#
                Measure mode lays the document out at the printable width so the height reported by
                a singlePage render is the height it will really occupy. Chromium otherwise measures
                at its own screen viewport, which is narrower and under-reports by about a fifth.
            #}
            {% if measure_width_mm is defined %}width: {{ measure_width_mm }}mm;{% endif %}
        }

        .pdf-header { margin-bottom: 8mm; }
        .pdf-header-rule {
            height: 0;
            border: 0;
            border-top: 2px solid #f5b400;
            margin: 0 0 6mm 0;
        }

        {% block extra_styles %}{% endblock %}
        {% if lyrics_sheets is defined and lyrics_sheets is not empty %}
            {% include 'pdf/song/_sheet_styles.html.twig' %}
        {% endif %}
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    {% block header %}{% endblock %}
    {% block body %}{% endblock %}
    {# « Inclure les paroles » (#1055): each song with lyrics, one per page after the list. #}
    {% for sheet in lyrics_sheets ?? [] %}
        {% include 'pdf/song/_sheet.html.twig' with {sheet: sheet} only %}
    {% endfor %}
</body>
</html>
